  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The colours of the flame are produced because of the movement of the electrons in the metal ions present in their salts. Calcium exhibits a&nbsp;brick-red colour. Strontium exhibits crimson colour. And the barium exhibits an apple green colour.&nbsp;</p><p>K is an&nbsp;alkali metal.&nbsp;Potassium is colourless or white but when it is heated, it produces a violet flame due to the excitation of the electrons to the higher energy orbitals. Potassium burns with a light purple-coloured flame.</p><p>So, the correct option is C</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
